 Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## Bounded learnability finding — unseen command code
+
+Protected-Racket counterexample: `counterexamples/review-7e311d7106d48a4b-command-map-ambiguity/evidence.json` (reproducer beside it). For seed 1 and sample indices 0..3, the three visible demonstrations use commands `4, 4, 0`, while the query uses command `2`. A rival program identical to the canonical rule except that command 2 means rotate-cw instead of rotate-180 matches every demonstration and changes the query. This is a finite lesson-level ambiguity, not a claim that every assembly fails.
+
+Recommended repair: assemble lessons so the query command is demonstrated on an asymmetric selected panel, or explicitly retain the alternative answer rather than expecting an unseen numeric command mapping to be inferred. The previously retained exact-override defect remains separate and unresolved.
